<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $28.22 bln on June 6.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $28.22 bln on June 6.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $28.22 billion on June 6 compared to $28.13 billion on May 30, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  June 6	May 30	 June 7</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     24,262	24,165	 16,852</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,954	 3,966	  4,509</p>
<p>    SDRs				     3	     3	    295</p>
<p>    Total			     28,219	28,134	 21,656</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
